course: dictionary
lesson: 12953
title: Exchangeable: swapping things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exchangeable describes something that can be swapped or traded for something else. Exchange means swap, so if you can exchange something, it is exchangeable.
explain: «The shop says this jumper is exchangeable within 28 days.» The words around exchangeable give the clue: you can take the jumper back and change it for a different size or colour, as long as you do it within 28 days.
explain: «These tickets are exchangeable but not refundable.» The word but shows a contrast. You can swap the tickets for others, but you cannot get your money back. Read the whole sentence to be sure of the meaning.
fact: Exchangeable means can be swapped or traded for something else.
fact: In shops, exchangeable goods can be taken back and changed for a different item, size or colour.
fact: Two useful phrases are «exchangeable for» and «exchangeable but not refundable».
fact: Coins are exchangeable for other money at a bank.
fact: In maths, 3 + 4 = 4 + 3: the numbers can be swapped round and the answer stays the same.
exercise: «The shop says this jumper is exchangeable within 28 days.» What does exchangeable mean here? | Can be worn only on Sundays | *Can be taken back and swapped for another size or colour | Too big to fit in the bag | Can be wrapped up as a gift
exercise: In 3 + 4 = 4 + 3, Sam says the numbers are exchangeable. What does he mean? | *The numbers can be swapped round and the answer stays the same | The answer gets bigger when they swap | The numbers are written in coins | The numbers can never change places
exercise: Ella says, «The coins are exchangeable for euros at the bank.» What does exchangeable mean? | Lost forever in the bank | Too old to use | Can be spent only in the shop next door | *Can be swapped for other money
test: «These tickets are exchangeable but not refundable.» What does not refundable mean? | The tickets are free | You must give the tickets to a friend | *You cannot get your money back | You can get your money back straight away
test: Which phrase means you can swap an item but cannot get your money back? | refundable and exchangeable | *exchangeable but not refundable | exchangeable for | exchangeable within 28 days
exam: Mia's receipt says «exchangeable within 28 days». Her jumper is too small. What should she do? | *Take it back within 28 days and swap it for a bigger size | Keep it forever without asking anyone | Throw it away because it is broken | Wash it again and hope it shrinks
